    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80188" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰχύ-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thick at the brim</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Henioch.
					1
				</span></i>
			 ; <i>with a large mouth</i>, of the oyster, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				304
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>speaking with a broad accent</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.
				ἢ τραχύστομοι</span>, of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κᾶρες
				βαρβαρόφωνοι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.2.28
			</span></i> :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰχυ-στομέω</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾰχυ-στομία</span></b> , ibid.</div>
